    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation for `POST /api/owners` (returned via `GET /api/owners/{id}`), satisfying the spec that when the request includes an ISO `birthDate`, the response returns `ageBand` as `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (65+), computed against `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `birthDate` (ISO date) input to the `OwnerFields` schema, and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` response schema. The DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`, `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum`) are generated from this spec at build time.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field (`birth_date` column) with getter/setter, so the value survives create\u2192GET.\n- **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on the hsqldb profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to be declared.\n- **`util/AgeBand.java`** \u2014 new helper computing the band from `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()`, returning `null` when no birth date is present.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping that computes `ageBand` from the entity's `birthDate`/`registrationDate` (yielding `null`, and thus an absent field, when no birth date was supplied). `birthDate` itself auto-maps by name from request\u2192entity\u2192response.\n\nThe wiring reuses the existing owner pipeline: `BuildOwner` runs `ownerMapper.toOwner(request)` (carrying `birthDate`), `SaveOwner` persists it, and the GET responder's `toOwnerDto` derives `ageBand`. No new function classes or YAML steps were needed since the value is derived, not validated.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (which posts `birthDate: 1990-01-01` and asserts `ageBand == ADULT` against the 2026 registration date) and the full suite both pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
